{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred shading deferred shading","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","fileName":"Deferred Shading.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deferred Shading","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Advanced Real-Time Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Advanced Real-Time Rendering","G-Buffer","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred shading deferred shading","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","fileName":"Deferred Shading.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deferred Shading","heading":"Deferred Shading","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Deferred shading separates surface rendering from lighting. The first pass writes visible surface properties into a [[G-Buffer]], and a later pass reads those screen-space values to evaluate global and local lights.\n\nThe approach avoids repeating complex geometry work for every light and performs well with many lights. It consumes substantial render-target memory and complicates transparency, which is commonly handled later with forward rendering.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Advanced Real-Time Rendering","G-Buffer","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred shading deferred shading","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Shading.md","fileName":"Deferred